  vignette: "A 29-year-old in her second trimester has a 9 mm soft, red, lobulated mass on the gingiva between 1.2 and 1.3. It bleeds when she brushes and has grown over 6 weeks. There is calculus on the adjacent teeth. The mass does not interfere with eating. The most appropriate management is:",
  options: ["Scaling and plaque control, deferring excision until after delivery","Urgent incisional biopsy for a suspected squamous cell carcinoma","A course of amoxicillin followed by review in 2 weeks","Excision to bone with curettage for a giant cell granuloma"],
