   "Facts: fast-growing, red, bleeding, gingival, with local plaque and calculus, in pregnancy. That is the picture of a pyogenic granuloma (pregnancy tumour).",
   "Cross out carcinoma: a young patient, a soft lobulated vascular mass and a clear local irritant point to a reactive lesion, not an indurated ulcer.",
